# Production origin, read by Vite at build time.
#
# This file IS committed, deliberately. The value is a public URL that ends up
# baked into every page's <link rel="canonical">, og:url, JSON-LD @id and
# sitemap.xml - it is not a secret, and hiding it would only mean every build
# silently falls back to root-relative canonicals, which is the failure
# assertSiteUrl() exists to prevent.
#
# Because the prerender bakes these URLs into static HTML, this must be correct
# at BUILD time. On Vercel that means either committing it here (done) or
# setting the same variable in the project's Environment Variables, which
# overrides this file.
#
# Normalised on read by src/seo/site.js through `new URL(raw).origin`, so a
# trailing slash is harmless. Canonical tags assume no trailing slash.
#
# When the real domain replaces the Vercel preview URL, change it here AND in the
# Vercel project's environment variables if one is set. A stale value is worse
# than none: canonical tags actively tell Google to consolidate your pages onto
# the wrong address.
#
# See .env.example for the format and the full rationale.
VITE_SITE_URL=https://fire-fighting-weld.vercel.app
